# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF on checkout, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites text files to
# CRLF as they land in the working tree. That breaks anything matching on a
# literal "\n": `tests/docs.rs` splits the examples on their `// docs:begin`
# markers to check the documentation quotes them verbatim, and a marker followed
# by "\r\n" is not the marker it is looking for.
* text=auto eol=lf
